/*
 * Real objects for the security, self-hosting and peer-to-peer diagrams (no "use client": server components use
 * these too). Every machine and service is drawn as the same kind of tile: a solid tile with one object on it,
 * two-tone (ink and sky), from Nucleo UI (18px glyph-duo). The registry is a server, the beacon an antenna, an agent
 * a laptop, a NAT a router, and so on, so a diagram reads as the things it shows rather than labelled boxes.
 *
 * The wiring helpers draw the lines between them as soft curves and rounded corners; packets travel along those
 * same paths with the sky kit's Beam (src/components/sky/beam.tsx), drawn in the same <svg>.
 */

